From: venera_d3d12
Subject: util/perf: write the CPU trace scopes as ETW events on Windows

Mesa's trace scopes (MESA_TRACE_SCOPE, VN_TRACE_FUNC, ...) compile to nothing on Windows, where neither Perfetto
nor atrace exists. Write them through ETW instead, with Venera's provider
{6ceeacf1-f746-4fe6-bff7-a596fede9b4e} in the layout Venera's UMDs use (begin: name, u64 value; end; counter:
name, i64 value), so a Venera trace (tests/win/venera-trace.exe) shows the driver's scopes on the same timeline
as the UMDs' events and the host's GPU work.

While no session listens, a scope costs one flag test: it no longer formats its name, which every
MESA_TRACE_SCOPE did before, with or without a backend.

diff -ruN a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build	2026-11-11 17:03:46.760845901 +0800
+++ b/meson.build	2026-11-11 17:04:20.176585583 +0800
@@ -2347,6 +2347,12 @@
   pre_args += '-DHAVE_GPUVIS'
 endif
 
+# Windows: the CPU trace macros write ETW events (src/util/perf/u_etw.c).
+with_etw = host_machine.system() == 'windows' and not with_perfetto
+if with_etw
+  pre_args += '-DHAVE_ETW'
+endif
+
 with_sysprof = get_option('sysprof')
 if with_sysprof
   dep_sysprof = dependency('sysprof-capture-4', version: '>= 49.0')
